From aaaf6c537f5cb524093a12e1e6a651403d44b830 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:21:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(terminal): every command result says how long it ran

A foreground command's result carries ran_for ("0.4s", "2m 14s"), and so
does a finished wait. The gateway's completion notice had no end time, so
its "Ran for" line never showed; it does now. Run times under 10 s keep a
tenth of a second.
---
 gateway/run_notifications.py            |  1 +
 tests/tools/test_process_run_time.py    | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/process_registry.py               |  5 +++-
 tools/process_registry_notifications.py |  8 +++--
 tools/terminal_tool.py                  |  4 ++-
 tools/terminal_tool_result.py           |  7 ++++-
 6 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gateway/run_notifications.py b/gateway/run_notifications.py
